.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-AWS-PUBLISH 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-aws-publish
.Nd make an EC2 image from a kldload disk, for running kldload as a hypervisor on AWS bare metal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar disk
.Op Fl -region Ar region
.Op Fl -bucket Ar name
.Op Fl -name Ar ami-name
.Op Fl -profile Ar profile
.Op Fl -description Ar text
.Op Fl -copy-regions Ar region , Ns Ar ...
.Op Fl -keep-s3
.Op Fl -no-seal
.Op Fl -dry-run
.Op Fl -json
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
turns a kldload disk \(em a file or a volume, in any format
.Xr qemu-img 1
reads \(em into an AMI that boots on EC2's bare-metal instance types, so
that kldload runs there as the host for virtual machines of its own.
In order it:
.Bl -enum -compact
.It
copies the disk to a raw image, since AWS does not import qcow2;
.It
seals the copy with
.Xr kldload-seal 8 ,
clearing the machine's identity; the source is never changed;
.It
uploads it to an S3 bucket, created if missing;
.It
imports it as an EBS snapshot, waiting 10 to 30 minutes;
.It
registers an AMI on that snapshot with ENA, SR-IOV and UEFI;
.It
optionally copies the AMI to other regions;
.El
.Pp
and removes the staged object from S3.
AWS credentials are whatever the
.Xr aws 1
command finds: environment, its credentials file, or an instance role.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -region Ar region
Default: the CLI's.
.It Fl -bucket Ar name
Default
.Ql kldload-export- Ns Ar account .
.It Fl -name Ar ami-name
Default
.Ql kldload- Ns Ar profile Ns - Ns Ar version Ns - Ns Ar timestamp .
.It Fl -profile Ar profile
The kldload profile to tag it with; default
.Ql kvm .
.It Fl -description Ar text
The AMI's description.
.It Fl -copy-regions Ar list
Copy the AMI to these regions too, separated by commas.
.It Fl -keep-s3
Leave the raw image in the bucket.
.It Fl -no-seal
Do not seal: a true copy of the machine, rarely what an AMI should be.
.It Fl -dry-run
Say each step without calling AWS or converting anything.
.It Fl -json
Progress as one JSON object a line on standard error, for the web
console.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 with each AMI's id on standard output, the first region's first; 1 on
a failure, named on standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop with no AWS command-line tool, on 2026-09-30, with
this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
